# Without this, `COPY . .` carries the host's `node_modules` into a Linux image.
# On a Windows or macOS machine those are the wrong binaries entirely — a
# Windows Prisma query engine and a host-specific Chromium — and the image would
# build successfully and then fail at runtime, which is the worst order to find
# out. Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image or has no business in
# one.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated in the image; copying it in risks shipping a stale
# artifact that nothing in the build would notice was stale.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated Prisma client — deliberately excluded. The image runs
# `prisma generate` itself so the query engine matches the container's platform
# rather than the developer's laptop.
database/generated

# Secrets. These must arrive as environment variables at run time, never baked
# into a layer: an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.docker.example

# Local and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.vercel
.claude
**/.claude
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
scratchpad
